From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.xaml: Frame and navigation, transition collections, relative dictionary sources

Windows Terminal's settings page did not open. Its MainPage has a Frame (contentFrame) that it navigates to each settings page, a ContentTransitions TransitionCollection with a NavigationThemeTransition, merged dictionaries named relative to its own file (CommonResources.xaml), and WinUI 2's NavigationView, whose MenuItems the markup replaced with its first item and whose collection raises CollectionChanged with NotifyCollectionChangedEventArgs; its FontIconSource makes icons through IFontIcon2.

Frame: Navigate (IFrame, IFrame2, IFrame5, INavigate) makes the page of a type (the application's through its metadata provider, or ours), calls OnNavigatedFrom/OnNavigatedTo, sets the page's Frame and Content and raises Navigated with NavigationEventArgs; GoBack/GoForward make the pages left again from their types and parameters. Navigating, NavigationFailed and NavigationStopped are kept, not raised; transitions are kept, not animated. Markup makes TransitionCollection, the theme transitions and the navigation transition infos. A merged dictionary's relative Source is relative to the file naming it. An item of a collection property a program registered goes into the collection it has. NotifyCollectionChangedEventArgs; FontIcon IsTextScaleFactorEnabled and MirroredWhenRightToLeft (kept).
---
